cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "Parameter Management Library of TUM Autonomous Motorsport"
type: software
abstract: >-
  param_management is a library for handling the large number of parameters in autonomous
  driving software without making the algorithm code depend on ROS 2. It provides a
  generic, dependency-free API supporting runtime parameter updates and all data types
  available in ROS 2, with C++ and Python bindings so that a mixed-language stack manages
  parameters uniformly. Optional helpers synchronise the parameters with the ROS 2
  parameter API, keeping them reachable via the ros2 param CLI at runtime while the
  algorithms themselves stay portable and testable outside ROS 2.
